From e8e2d25fbe9c775b11a3a9e8548cde5a8ba33351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:39:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix wrong exit data set of merged blocks and wrong exit block
 after value select expansion

MergeBasicBlocks appends a single entry successor to its predecessor
and, since 83e805b, copies the successor's exit data set so the merged
block keeps its exit values. The copy was made after mTrueJump had
already been advanced, so the merged block took the data set of the
block beyond the one it absorbed, and dereferenced a null pointer when
the absorbed block had no successor. PutJump uses that set to turn a
trailing JMP into a conditional branch when the Z or C flag is known,
and with the wrong set it emitted a never taken BEQ for a nested
conditional such as c ? 3 : (d ? 4 : 5), so the function fell off its
end with native code generation. Copy the data set before advancing
mTrueJump.

The null dereference happened when the final MergeBasicBlocks absorbed
the block holding the temporary RTS, which is only possible because
ExpandADCToBranch, after splitting the exit block for a value select,
handed the exit block role to the first arm of the new branch instead of
the block that received the trailing instructions. Since fb67321 the RTS
was therefore removed from the wrong block, and a function whose exit
block still held a value select, such as a store of p ? 242 : -127 at
its end, returned early and skipped its stores at every optimization
level; 83e805b turned that silent miscompile into the crash. Hand the
role to the first block behind the branch without successors, which is
the block that inherited the exit block's missing successors along with
the temporary RTS, and assert that the instruction removed as the
temporary RTS is one.

Adds two regression tests. Both fail with -n at every optimization
level before the fix, the first with a wrong result, the second with
the compiler crash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J5rsu7nnbQYnRY7GP34gdn
---
